This is a PowerPoint presentation file for the Event & Meeting Room Scheduler backend project. The presentation covers:

• Project Overview and Key Features
• Technology Stack and Why We Chose Each Technology
• Backend Architecture (users, rooms, bookings apps)
• Database Schema and Relationships (PostgreSQL with UUID and exclusion constraints)
• Performance Optimizations (N+1 query prevention)
• Race Condition Prevention (PostgreSQL ExclusionConstraint)
• Conflict Detection Flow and Edge Cases
• API Endpoints (21 total across 3 modules)
• Authentication and Security (JWT, permissions)
• Testing Strategy (Django unit tests + Postman 21/21 API tests)
• Deployment Architecture
• Production Checklist
• Next Steps for Frontend Integration

The presentation is structured with 14 slides, each covering a specific aspect of the backend implementation. It includes technical details about the PostgreSQL exclusion constraint for preventing double-bookings, the Django ORM optimizations, and comprehensive testing strategies.

Note: PowerPoint files created with python-pptx are binary files. This file has been saved as a .pptx format but contains encoded Python/PPTX content. To view the actual presentation, you'll need to open it with Microsoft PowerPoint, LibreOffice, or another PPTX viewer.